  "Question": "Find the inradius of a right triangle with legs 5 and 12.",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "2",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The hypotenuse is 13, and \\(r=(5+12-13)/2=2\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Use the inradius as a common height\n\nJoining the incenter to the three vertices divides the triangle into three smaller triangles, each with height equal to the inradius \\(r\\) when its original side is used as the base. The hypotenuse is \\(\\sqrt{5^2+12^2}=13\\). Equating the whole area to the sum of the smaller areas gives\n\\[\n\\frac{5\\times12}{2}=\\frac{5r}{2}+\\frac{12r}{2}+\\frac{13r}{2}=15r.\n\\]\nThus \\(30=15r\\), and the inradius is \\(r=2\\).",
